    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup is anchored by **Tyler Freeman**, who earns the top spot on our board with a 71.22 score, buoyed significantly by a favorable matchup against Ray and a top-of-the-order assignment that maximizes his scoring potential. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** remains a high-floor play at 70.46, as he benefits from a premier matchup against Kochanowicz\u2019s 5.17 xERA; his ability to leverage the platoon advantage in a hitter-friendly environment makes him a foundational piece for this slate. While our focus remains on maximizing stolen base opportunities, the core of our offense\u2014including **Matt Chapman**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Lawrence Butler**\u2014all cleared the 65-point threshold by exploiting the sluggish delivery of Gordon, T, who offers significant swipe potential for our aggressive baserunners today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was undoubtedly **Bryson Stott**, who hovered near the 51-point mark. While his metrics against right-handed pitching were solid, he ultimately lost his spot to the higher offensive ceilings provided by our starting infielders. We continue to monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh**, who remains sidelined on the IL, as his absence continues to press our depth at the catcher position. Investors should also note the risk associated with **Daulton Varsho**; despite a strong park factor, his score is tempered to 57.53 due to a challenging matchup against Bradish and a cautionary tag regarding an elite hold pitcher who may stifle our attempts to pad the stolen base category. Given the 5x5 Roto constraints, we are prioritizing the efficiency of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Gavin Sheets** to keep us competitive in AVG and HR while we hunt for steals against the slower-working arms on today\u2019s docket.",
